          "intro": "Culture isn\u2019t fixed in time. It is inherited and reinterpreted, questioned and created, lived and shared.\n\nUrban Suburban Perspectives works across Heritage, Art and Culture, exploring how what we inherit continues to find meaning in contemporary life."
        },
        "hidden": false,
        "id": "8b9e00d593ec4da9af5f1f5a301a725b",
        "styles": {},
        "type": "hero"
      },
      {
        "data": {
          "body_html": "<p>A place, a building, a story, a tradition or a way of making can hold meaning far beyond where it began.</p><p>USP brings together people, knowledge and different perspectives to explore how these inheritances can remain meaningful in the present\u2014and become a starting point for new ideas, creative expression and opportunity.</p><p>Across Heritage, Art and Culture, the work takes different forms, each shaped by its own context and the people involved. Through it, people can develop skills, share knowledge, shape what is created and open new pathways to livelihood.</p>",
          "eyebrow": "Who We Are",
          "heading": "Heritage, Art and Culture \u2014 Kept in Motion.",
          "style": "columns"
        },
        "hidden": false,
        "id": "9acbb2583dfc483ab0f1a5654ac1786f",
        "styles": {},
        "type": "text"
      },
